WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:05.480
Autumn clouds float in the blue sky.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.090
Having done our fill of eating,

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.740
reading manga and playing sports,

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.240
we celebrated the arts this fall.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.080
You want me to draw a manga?

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.720
Y-Yes. Twice a year, the Manga Society...

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.430
collects manga we've drawn in an anthology.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:28.850
Really?

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.340
So they do some club like activities...

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:32.940
at the Manga Society.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.090
Sorry?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.600
I was enjoying its half-going 
home club style.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.600
But even if I agree to draw a manga,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.100
I don't own a beret.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.230
You don't need a beret to draw manga.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.570
I don't own a striped shirt or 
 have an F in the middle of my name.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.950
You don't need any of those.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.020
Please make your manga at least five pages long.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.960
If you have any questions, just ask.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.940
Um, who are you?

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.470
I'm a first year. Ryunosuke M-Matsushita.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.970
A-Anyway, see what you can do.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.900
Those look great.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.380
Shun-chan, can I have one?

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.780
Go ahead.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.360
What'd you bring those with you 
for? What are you, a girl?

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.590
Can I have one, too?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.910
So...

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.000
You're all going to draw a manga for me.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:15.130
Daily Wage Hero

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.490
What? B-But why?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.230
Is this why you had us come here?

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:20.800
Yes.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.710
Isn't this <i>your</i> club activity?

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.410
We've got nothing to do with it.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.330
Yeah, but listen...

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.770
I only read manga.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.080
I don't ever draw them.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.150
That's why we'll draw in the relay format.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:41.990
We'll each draw one page and 
combine them to create one story.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.370
Ah, I'll do it.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.910
Sounds interesting, doesn't it?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:47.520
Yes.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.330
I'll pass out the paper.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.990
I'll pass. I don't draw.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.330
Hey, hey, hey.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.620
Don't say stuff that'll undermine our teamwork

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.510
when we're about to start a group project.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.210
We don't know the first thing about teamwork.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.100
What should it be about?

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.910
Let's see...

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:09.790
How about a sports manga?

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.800
A sports comedy?

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.600
Don't you think that'd be hard to draw?

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:17.190
It might be difficult for you 
if you're too stupid to realize...

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.240
that he meant a serious sports story.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.650
I'd prefer a fantasy story with wizards.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.220
You would.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.620
You're a little fantastical yourself.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.630
Why don't we draw a love comedy documenting...

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.680
the love between Kaname and his mom?

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.180
That wouldn't be a comedy.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.580
It's too taboo.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.620
What if someone spotted them?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:45.100
At the Tsukahara family that she works for, the mother and son are...

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.100
Enough!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.040
You're making this too complicated.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.410
Why not stick to

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.420
the simple, classic adventure of a hero,

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.620
with a demon king and monsters?

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.130
A hero...

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.460
An adventure...

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.430
I see.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.770
We've been forgetting 
the all important genre.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:06.030
The adventure of an ambitious and brave 
hero is at the core of our youth.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:10.780
Okay, let's give it a try.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.160
Our first artist is Yutan!

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.710
Yukki will be second!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:22.000
Shun-chan is third, and I'll go fourth!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.470
Kanamecchi will draw the 
fifth and final page!

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.430
Isn't this exciting?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.730
Kanamecchi, you'll have to carry 
our efforts over the finish line...

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.120
with an emotional conclusion.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.230
Yeah, I'll carry all of your 
failures to a pathetically weak finish.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.850
I finished the first page.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.490
Finally!

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.240
How does it start?

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.830
This is good!

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:51.490
Yuta-kun, I didn't know you drew!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:56.560
I don't, but I grew up in a room overflowing 
with the rafters with Yuki's manga.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.720
It's only natural this would happen.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.000
No, it's not.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.910
This is amazing.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:04.210
His costume and sword are awesome.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.660
Hey, who are these two 
standing next to the hero?

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:12.460
The country's best spearman 
and a sexy magician.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.680
It's perfect. This is what boys want.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:17.800
Are you stupid?

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.650
What are you trying to 
say about innocent boys?

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.510
But I think it's a great start.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.550
It is, isn't it?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:31.660
Yukki, keep this going and 
draw something awesome.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.410
I'm done with the second page.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.280
What?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.680
Who's this? What's up with that outfit?

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.380
A convenience store? He's 
going to a convenience store?

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.940
What happened between the 
first and second pages?

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:54.000
Yuta's costume was too hard to draw.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.640
I simplified it and ended up with this.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.180
What did you have to simplify 
to turn him into this?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:04.870
You'd have to simplify your costs to 
make such a low budget hero.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:09.750
The sword you worked so hard 
on looks kind of sad instead.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.670
They couldn't be more mismatched.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.490
Huh?

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.120
His two friends are missing. Where are they?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:16.960
They died.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:17.750
Already?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.750
It took all my effort to draw one character.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:26.750
That's why they're telling 
him to keep going strong.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.090
There's nothing strong about this speech bubble.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:31.820
He's crushing them under there.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:34.090
You're hopeless, Yukki.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:36.670
Shun-chan, it's up to you now.

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.250
I'll do my best.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.350
I'm done with the third page.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.740
The hero's eyes are huge.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:48.320
Despite the loss of his 
friends, the hero doesn't give up...

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.860
and fixes his gaze on what's ahead in this scene.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:56.610
With those eyes, he's not 
just looking ahead.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:08:01.750
The bitterness of losing his friends to monsters 
has made made the hero even stronger.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.250
No, he lost his friends to your artistic skills.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.680
I introduced a new character, too.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.280
Exactly what part of this guy in a t-Shirt 
made him seem like a hero to her?

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.600
She probably spotted his sword 
with those huge eyes of hers.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.580
Help me, Mister Hero!

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:20.290
My sister has been kidnapped by monsters!

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.730
What did you say?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:25.190
It's all right. I'll save her.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.070
That's right.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:30.280
A hero has to fight monsters.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.280
Well? Can you feel the intensity?

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:38.710
He wouldn't last long.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.290
Two more pages, huh?

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:47.570
The story's coming along 
pretty well, isn't it?

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:50.830
It looks like he's headed 
towards saving the world.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:55.300
I don't think the world expects 
anything from this hero.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.750
It's my turn, isn't it?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.880
Maybe I'll try drawing a battle scene.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:01.920
Asaba-kun.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:04.640
There's a first year looking for you.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.810
H-Hello.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:10.320
I came to see how your 
work is coming along.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.220
H-How are you doing?

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:15.010
Do you have any questions?

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:20.280
I don't know what the hero 
wants to do any more.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.370
What?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.540
Is this the work of the other club members?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.150
Yes.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:28.300
Huh? Am I behind?

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.250
No, um...

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:31.920
Sorry.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.230
I know I'm holding you up,

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:37.170
but you won't believe a Manga Society 
member could have drawn my pages.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.850
It's fine.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:41.970
You've never really felt 
like a member of the club.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:47.710
I mean, not in a bad way.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:55.750
Y-You like manga and anime, but you 
don't seem like an otaku at all.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:59.570
N-Not to mention how cool you are, so...

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.080
Huh?

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:06.970
I, um... S-Sorry.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:08.600
It's fine.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:12.270
What?

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:17.340
Nothing. Just got the feeling I got 
a little peek at the pages of youth.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.280
The what?

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.340
Nevermind, nevermind.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.900
This is the bittersweetness of our...

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:25.770
That's it!

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.890
I finished the fourth page.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:31.400
Really?

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:36.040
What? The hero's wearing a school uniform?

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:37.640
Forget the adventure.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.530
We'll go with a different theme.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.610
What?

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.200
Are you stupid?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.550
You can't change the genre now.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:48.920
A hero sprinting with bread in his mouth...

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:51.170
seems plenty adventurous to me.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:56.980
Everyone, we've forgotten all 
about an important genre.

00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:57.600
That is...

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:00.880
the school drama!

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.890
Even if we draw a heroic adventure, 
it'll be nothing more than fantasy.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:10.700
But the friendship, hard work and conflict...

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:15.860
experienced in our adolescence are
 a reality that only now we can draw.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.220
Friendship.

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:18.370
Hard work.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.610
Conflict.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.280
Are you stupid?

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:26.000
We're not actually living that 
life, so it's completely unrelated!

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.430
It's okay. Use your imagination.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:31.250
So, it's imaginary either way.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:35.150
A high school girl...

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:38.230
She's my ideal heroine.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.860
This hero's hair looks 
just like someone else's.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:42.840
Really?

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.310
Don't worry about the details.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:47.070
What? Already?

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.680
Why are they getting married so quickly?

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.870
Okay, okay. Kanamecchi, you're next.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:54.000
It's the last page.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:55.830
You can do it.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:59.820
Something about your support pisses me off.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:03.950
Here. I finished the fifth page.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:27.920
Tsukahara-san, the setting's 
suddenly changed to Mars.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.770
Kaname-kun, you really are 
the best at everything.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:34.230
Best at what? Sorry I suck at drawing.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.670
Shun, you can do it.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:40.170
If you don't say something, who will?

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.990
Forget about that panel. Keep reading.

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.450
It wraps up really nicely.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:53.570
The celebrated newlyweds create
a physical embodiment of their love...

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:58.030
and so the baton of life is passed on.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:02.050
Stop looking at that panel.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.970
We finished all five pages.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:11.860
It was a lot of work, but 
I'm glad we finished.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:16.420
Drawing a manga in the relay format was pretty fun.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:18.800
Let's switch up the order 
and do it again some time.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:21.460
Change the members before 
you change the order.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:25.590
U-Um, I'm sorry.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:26.620
For what?

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:32.810
I just figured we might have made 
something you're not happy with.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:38.040
I wouldn't say that.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:42.220
I could never have drawn 
five pages by myself.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.480
Thanks for your help.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:45.870
Yuki-kun.

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:53.930
Yukki, let's go to the faculty 
office and make copies for all of us.

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:04.880
What are you doing?

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:09.030
Our first collaboration ended.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.760
Why is the bottom cut off?

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:19.000
A couple of people got really angry.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.960
As though appalled by our foray 
into the unfamiliar arts,

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:28.160
the bored autumn clouds drifted away.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.360
I have a hero I admire.

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:48.950
Most heroes come from a 
faraway place in the cosmos,

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.630
but he...

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:53.370
You want me to draw a manga?

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.370
Y-Yes.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.120
A-Anyway, see what you can do.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:10.380
Senpai and Me

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.220
<b>Manga Society</b>

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.170
Did you ask him to do it?

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:18.990
Yes.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:19.730
Well?

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.770
He listened earnestly to what I had to say.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.110
I think he'll do it.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:26.360
Really?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.430
That's amazing.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.650
This might actually sell.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.990
It might even sell out.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.680
I wonder what he'll draw.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.880
Probably a sports story.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.880
The protagonist will join the Basketball Club...

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.570
...make friends...

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:42.130
...and with a boy like Tsukahara-kun...

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.330
I wanna read it now.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.050
If it sells, I guess.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.580
I know, right?

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.740
<i>He's not that sort of hero.</i>

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:59.000
I'm going to write about Yuki-senpai.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:05.990
I wonder what I should write. A hero is...

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.940
The cake is ours.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:12.870
Stop!

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:13.570
What?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:20.270
Team Skull, I won't let you harm the Earth.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:22.870
Transform!

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:30.880
Hero Blue!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.510
Hero Yellow!

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.140
Hero Black!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.770
Hero Pink!

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:45.400
Hero Red!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:49.670
Together, we are...

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:52.110
High School Fighting Homa Rangers!{F: Homa? Bahaha, why not just Homo?}

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.030
So cool.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.740
That's what I'll write.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:01.250
The five of them pose together, and...

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.810
Together, we are...

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:05.530
High School Fighting Homa Rangers!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.040
Why are you wearing your school uniform?

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:14.140
I can't pull off full body tights.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.010
These aren't full body tights!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:18.050
I'm surprised you guys wore them.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.780
Please continue teaching the kids...

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:25.340
in front of the TV the 
true meaning of bravery.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.340
Don't call it bravery!

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:30.160
Th-This is getting really embarrassing.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.320
Stop it.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:34.450
We're a team. We can't afford to fight now.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:35.980
You're right.

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:37.200
All right, everyone.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:40.170
Let's work together to defeat our enemies.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.580
You have to fight, too.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.110
<i>Maybe I'll try something else.</i>

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.090
<i>What else would suit Yuki-senpai?</i>

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:03.910
Old man, I'm taking this girl 
until you pay your debts.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:04.870
Dad!

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:05.740
Oshun!

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:06.570
Hold it right there.

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:12.330
You're the child-toting samurai!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.740
If you must take someone...

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:24.500
Take him.

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.610
He's just been a pain in the neck.

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:30.250
He's too heavy to take anywhere.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.910
<i>I can't come up with anything good.</i>

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.010
S-Sorry.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.140
Senpai.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.710
Oh, perfect.

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:48.270
I don't think I'll be done 
with my work any time soon.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.490
That's fine.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.560
I'm not close to finishing at all.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.900
Really?

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.010
That's no good, Matsushita-kun.

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.290
You can do it.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:03.270
Asaba-senpai is so cool.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:08.730
Yuta-senpai's so great, but 
Yuki-senpai has a dark side.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.630
His lone wolf attitude is so cool.

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:13.420
<i>That's it!</i>

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:16.740
You again, Asaba?

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:19.680
If you get in trouble 
again, you'll be expelled.

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:30.190
You're alone, too.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.520
Stop it.

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:42.440
What do you want?

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:45.570
What do you think you're...

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:51.670
I saw a lonely puppy shivering in the rain.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:55.920
Yes.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.770
<i>This is great.</i>

00:19:57.770 --> 00:19:59.380
<i>I'll go with this.</i>

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.390
I can't agree to this.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:09.020
A girl like you isn't suited 
to be with a brute like Asaba.

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:10.770
Stop it, Tsukahara-kun.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:14.020
Yuki's not that kind of person.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:16.020
Don't say bad things about him.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.570
It seems you took care of our Mon recently.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:23.800
I've come to thank you.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.010
Boss, get him.

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:30.080
Looks like you've got a 
cutie with you today.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.080
Come here.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.790
Don't touch my girl.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.050
Stop it.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:47.240
Please, I don't want to see 
you get hurt any more.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:48.850
Let go, Matsuoka.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:49.980
No.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:50.810
Let go.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.420
No!

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:51.980
Let go!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:52.600
No!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.870
Let go!

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.190
There's an anime at five I want to watch.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:03.700
What?

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:15.780
<i>That's weird. Why can't I draw anything?</i>

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:18.090
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:20.590
Hello.

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:24.620
Senpai, what are you doing here?

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:28.620
I pissed off my class's "four-eyes."

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:29.910
I'm hiding from him.

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:32.020
What are you actually doing?

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:40.190
Could it be Yuki-senpai isn't heroic at all?

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:43.090
Is that why my stories turn out that way?

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:44.070
Watch out!

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:52.000
Senpai, thank you.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:54.960
Excuse me. Can we have our ball back please?

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.950
I have a hero I admire.

00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:16.280
Most heroes come from a 
faraway place in the cosmos,

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:20.730
but he's not from such a distant place as that.

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:23.730
Probably because it'd be too much effort.

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.510
But I still think he's 
greater than any hero.

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:37.970
Let me see your manga when you're 
done with it, Matsushita-kun.

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:39.510
Yes!
